quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  11,63,"He said: ‘O my people! Just tell me: If I did have clear proof from my Lord, and He had granted me mercy from Himself, then who would protect me from Allah if I disobeyed Him? For then, you would increase me in nothing but loss."
  11,64,"O my people! This She-camel of Allah is a sign for you. So leave her free to graze in Allah’s land. And do not cause her any harm. For then, a prompt punishment will overtake you.’"
  11,65,"But they slew her, and he said: ‘Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days. That is a warning not to be proved false.’"
  11,66,"So, when Our command (of punishment) came, We saved Salih and those who believed along with him by a mercy from Us, and (We saved them) from the disgrace of that day. Your Lord is indeed the All-Strong, the All-Mighty."
  11,67,"The dreadful Blast overtook those who were wrongdoers. And they became lifeless bodies in their abodes,"
  11,68,as if they had never lived there. Yes! The Thamud disbelieved in their Lord. So away with the Thamud!
  11,69,"Indeed, Our messengers came to Ibrahim (Abraham) with glad tidings (and) said: ‘Peace (be on you).’ He replied: ‘Peace (be on you).’ Then, without any delay, he brought in a roasted calf (for them)."
  11,70,"When he saw their hands not reaching towards it, he became suspicious about them and conceived a fear of them (on account of them not having the meal). They said: ‘Do not be afraid. We have been sent to the people of Lut (Lot).’"
  11,71,"His wife (Sara) was standing (nearby), and she laughed.* Then We gave her glad tidings of (the birth of) Ishaq (Isaac), and after Ishaq (Isaac), (glad tidings) of Ya‘qub (Jacob)."
